# L §5.10 Value, LOAD-PRICE for a place of unit any: buy's leg eur writes EUR into broker, which load sees, so
# value(broker, d) in PLN with no by is refused at load, at its line (L §8.4 R-load: "no run meets a fault load could
# see"; tally 2.1.7 R5, the review's finding 3, pick P41). Until 2.1.7 refcore refused it at run, with no line, when
# the run had booked the EUR.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
unit EUR: currency minor 0.01

kind brokerages: place any min 0
kind fx_buys: event certain
  leg eur: EUR
  leg cash: PLN

input pxp[u in currencies]: num PLN/u
input buy_day: date
input eur_amt: money EUR
input pln_amt: money PLN

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place eurkonto: accounts EUR lives 2026-01-01..
place market: outside lives 1900-01-01..

move buy: fx_buys
  on buy_day
  leg eur from market to broker amount eur_amt
  leg cash from konto to market amount pln_amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  brokerages + [broker] lives 2026-01-01..
  pxp[EUR] = none
  buy_day = 2026-03-02
  eur_amt = 100.00 EUR
  pln_amt = 425.00 PLN
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"

ask rp: value(broker, 2026-06-30) in PLN
=== expect
refused: LOAD-PRICE value(broker) in PLN holds units in EUR and states no by (m.tally:41)
